## 4. Digital Twin Integration

The DCM is specified and evaluated entirely within the v4.0 digital twin environment. No code runs on physical hardware; no sensors collect real-world data; no actuators have been commanded. The digital twin augments the single-vessel simulation with a multi-vessel scenario generator and a configurable communication model.

### 4.1 Communication Model

Links are simulated with configurable latency (100–500 ms), packet loss rate (0–30%), and bandwidth per link (1–10 kB s⁻¹). These parameters span the realistic operating range of VHF data, LTE, and satellite links; they are not validated against any measured maritime channel, and real-world performance may differ.

### 4.2 Cognitive Token Structure

Each vessel's Π layer broadcasts a 168-byte JSON token at 1 Hz:

```json
{
  "vessel_id": 3,
  "timestamp": 1718400000.123,
  "lamport_clock": 942,
  "belief_entropy": 0.23,
  "intent_vector": {
    "alpha": 0.5, "beta": 0.2, "gamma": 0.2,
    "delta": 0.05, "epsilon": 0.05
  },
  "strategic_reference": {
    "waypoint": [37.7749, -122.4194],
    "speed": 20.0,
    "formation_offset": [0.0, 50.0]
  },
  "coherence_score": 0.96,
  "risk_bounds": {
    "min_separation": 50.0,
    "max_speed_variance": 0.1
  }
}
```

At 168 bytes per second per vessel, the bandwidth demand is negligible even for fleets of 100+ vessels on a 9.6 kbps VHF link. Whether this token structure is sufficient for real-world coordination under adversarial conditions is an open question that physical trials would need to resolve.

### 4.3 Distributed Belief Propagation

Each Π layer runs a distributed Bayesian filter that fuses local EKF observations with received neighbour tokens. The filter is a damped variant of loopy belief propagation over the communication graph; damping ensures convergence despite cycles. Because tokens carry abstracted cognitive states rather than raw sensor streams, the filter is robust to moderate latency and loss in simulation. Robustness under real maritime electromagnetic conditions has not been evaluated.

