## 6. Simulation Predictions (Digital Twin Only)

The following results are digital twin simulation predictions obtained from 10,000 randomised fleet missions (3–15 vessels, JONSWAP sea states $H_s \in [0.2, 2.5]$ m, wind gusts, GPS dropouts, communication partitions at rates described in Section 4.1). They are predictions, not measured outcomes. All figures carry the implicit caveat that real-world performance may differ — potentially substantially — due to sensor noise, hull manufacturing tolerances, unmodelled hydrodynamic interactions, and communication channel behaviour not captured by the simulation model. These numbers should be interpreted as evidence of theoretical feasibility, not as performance guarantees.

| Scenario | Metric | Independent OCA (baseline) | DCM (predicted) | Predicted improvement |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 10-vessel convoy, $H_s = 1.2$ m | Collision risk (fraction of missions with any pair within 30 m) | 8.2% | 4.8% | −41% |
| 15-vessel search pattern, $H_s = 2.0$ m | Fleet energy (Wh/NM-vessel) | 185 | 133 | −28% |
| Communication partition (5 min, 3 vessels) | Coherence restoration time | N/A | 11.2 s | — |
| 30% random token loss | Mission completion rate | 92.1% | 96.7% | +4.6 pp |
