The predicted 28% energy improvement arises from the fleet-level optimisation of V-formation geometry in the simulation, which reduces modelled wave drag by 9% and allows vessels to surf each other's simulated wakes. Whether this benefit materialises in real irregular sea conditions — where formation geometry is harder to maintain — is unknown. The predicted 41% collision risk reduction reflects the token-based intent sharing resolving ambiguous encounter geometries in simulation; actual reduction depends on communication reliability and vessel response latency in hardware.

