## Appendix B: Proof That Local Adjunctions Lift to a Global Swarm Adjunction

**Proposition:** Given local adjunctions $F_i \dashv G_i$ for each vessel $i$, and belief-transfer functors $T_{ij}$ satisfying the pseudo-functor structure of Appendix A.4, there exist functors:

$$F_\text{swarm} : \mathbf{C}_{\Pi,\text{swarm}} \to \mathbf{C}_{\Sigma,\text{swarm}}, \qquad G_\text{swarm} : \mathbf{C}_{\Sigma,\text{swarm}} \to \mathbf{C}_{\Pi,\text{swarm}}$$

forming an adjunction $F_\text{swarm} \dashv G_\text{swarm}$.

**Proof:**

Define $F_\text{swarm}$ on objects as follows. Given a descent datum $\{(\pi_i, \phi_{ij})\} \in \mathbf{C}_{\Pi,\text{swarm}}$, set:

$$F_\text{swarm}\bigl(\{(\pi_i, \phi_{ij})\}\bigr) = \bigl\{\bigl(F_i(\pi_i),\ \tilde{\phi}_{ij}\bigr)\bigr\}$$

where $\tilde{\phi}_{ij}: T_{\Sigma,ij}(F_i(\pi_i)) \xrightarrow{\sim} F_j(\pi_j)$ is the image of $\phi_{ij}$ under $F_j$ composed with the natural isomorphism $T_{\Sigma,ij} \circ F_i \cong F_j \circ T_{\Pi,ij}$ that holds by the pseudo-functoriality of $T$ and the naturality of the local adjunctions. The cocycle condition for $\tilde{\phi}_{ij}$ follows from the cocycle condition for $\phi_{ij}$ and the functoriality of $F_j$. Therefore $F_\text{swarm}$ is well-defined on objects of the descent category.

Define $G_\text{swarm}$ symmetrically using the right adjoints $G_i$ and the coherence isomorphisms $T_{\Pi,ij} \circ G_i \cong G_j \circ T_{\Sigma,ij}$.

To establish the adjunction, we must construct a natural bijection:

$$\text{Hom}_{\mathbf{C}_{\Sigma,\text{swarm}}}\bigl(F_\text{swarm}(\Pi_\bullet),\ \Sigma_\bullet\bigr) \cong \text{Hom}_{\mathbf{C}_{\Pi,\text{swarm}}}\bigl(\Pi_\bullet,\ G_\text{swarm}(\Sigma_\bullet)\bigr)$$

A morphism $f: F_\text{swarm}(\Pi_\bullet) \to \Sigma_\bullet$ in $\mathbf{C}_{\Sigma,\text{swarm}}$ is a family of local morphisms $\{f_i: F_i(\pi_i) \to \sigma_i\}$ compatible with the coherence isomorphisms. By the local adjunction $F_i \dashv G_i$, each $f_i$ corresponds uniquely to a morphism $\bar{f}_i: \pi_i \to G_i(\sigma_i)$ in $\mathbf{C}_{\Pi,i}$. The family $\{\bar{f}_i\}$ is compatible with the descent coherence isomorphisms if and only if $\{f_i\}$ is, by the naturality of the local adjunctions. Therefore the family $\{\bar{f}_i\}$ defines a morphism $\Pi_\bullet \to G_\text{swarm}(\Sigma_\bullet)$ in $\mathbf{C}_{\Pi,\text{swarm}}$, and the correspondence is a natural bijection. ∎

**Corollary:** The unit $\eta_\text{swarm}: \text{id} \Rightarrow G_\text{swarm} \circ F_\text{swarm}$ and counit $\varepsilon_\text{swarm}: F_\text{swarm} \circ G_\text{swarm} \Rightarrow \text{id}$ of the global adjunction are given componentwise by the local units and counits $\{\eta_i\}$ and $\{\varepsilon_i\}$ respectively. The fleet coherence score $\rho_\text{fleet}(t)$ is therefore the normalised $\ell^1$ norm of the family of counit residuals $\{\|\varepsilon_{\sigma_i} - \sigma_i\|\}$, as defined in Section 3.2. ∎

