## Appendix D: Fleet Mode Transition Automaton

The swarm-wide meta-cognitive authority $\mathcal{M}_\text{swarm}$ is formally a finite-state automaton $\mathcal{A}_\text{fleet} = (Q, \Sigma_\text{ev}, \delta, q_0, F_\text{accept})$ where:

- $Q = \{\text{Coherent},\ \text{Disjoint},\ \text{Partitioned},\ \text{Emergency}\}$ are the fleet modes.
- $\Sigma_\text{ev}$ is the set of observable events: $\{e_1: \rho_\text{fleet} \leq \theta_\text{fleet},\ e_2: \rho_\text{fleet} > \theta_\text{fleet},\ e_3: H_{\Pi,i} > \theta_\Pi \text{ for some } i,\ e_4: \text{graph partitioned},\ e_5: \text{graph reconnected},\ e_6: \rho_\text{fleet} \leq \theta_\text{crit} \text{ or Mode 3 triggered}\}$.
- $q_0 = \text{Coherent}$ is the initial state.
- The transition function $\delta$ is:

| Current Mode | Event | Next Mode | Action |
|---|---|---|---|
| Coherent | $e_1$ or $e_3$ | Disjoint | Affected vessels enter Mode 2; neighbours inflate safety margins |
| Coherent | $e_6$ | Emergency | All vessels enter Mode 3; disperse to holding points |
| Disjoint | $e_2$ | Coherent | Resume full token coordination |
| Disjoint | $e_4$ | Partitioned | Each component runs independent DCM |
| Disjoint | $e_6$ | Emergency | All vessels enter Mode 3 |
| Partitioned | $e_5$ | Disjoint | Reconcile belief states via Lamport timestamp merge |
| Partitioned | $e_6$ | Emergency | All vessels enter Mode 3 |
| Emergency | $e_2$ and all vessels exit Mode 3 | Coherent | Restore full coordination |

The automaton is **deterministic** — no two transitions from the same state share the same trigger event — and **live** — from every state there exists a path back to Coherent, preventing permanent lock-in to degraded modes. The Emergency-to-Coherent transition requires both $\rho_\text{fleet} > \theta_\text{fleet}$ and confirmation that all vessels have exited their local Mode 3, preventing premature restoration.

**Formal safety property:** The automaton satisfies the invariant that in Emergency mode, all actuation authority resides in the hardware Reflex layers. This is enforced not by the automaton itself but by the physical isolation of the Reflex layer on each vessel — the automaton has no write access to the Reflex MCU. The automaton can only observe vessel states and broadcast fleet-mode tokens; local hardware authority is always preserved.

