## Appendix G: Relationship to the Distributed Cognitive Orchestration Framework

The DCM is an instantiation of the Distributed Cognitive Orchestration (DCO) framework (Maakoul, 2024–2026), the primary dissertation framework of which this work is a component. The mapping between DCO constructs and DCM constructs is as follows:

| DCO Construct | DCM Instantiation |
|---|---|
| Heterogeneous agent | Autonomous hydrofoil vessel with OCA stack |
| Agent cognitive state | Tuple $(\pi_i, \sigma_i, \mu_i) \in C_{\Pi,i} \times C_{\Sigma,i} \times C_{\mathcal{M},i}$ |
| Orchestration graph | Communication graph $\mathcal{G} = (\mathcal{V}, \mathcal{E})$ |
| Inter-agent coupling operator | Belief-transfer functor $T_{ij}$ |
| Collective cognitive state | Descent data of the fibred category $\mathcal{F}$ |
| Orchestration cost functional | Fleet cost $J_\text{swarm}$ including coordination penalty $\Phi$ |
| Global cognitive coherence | Fleet coherence score $\rho_\text{fleet}(t)$ |
| Graceful degradation hierarchy | Fleet mode automaton $\mathcal{A}_\text{fleet}$ |

The DCM therefore serves as a concrete test case for the DCO framework in the maritime domain, providing: (a) a specific realisation of the abstract DCO inter-agent coupling operator as a category-theoretic belief-transfer functor; (b) a concrete instantiation of the DCO global coherence metric as $\rho_\text{fleet}$; and (c) a physical domain in which the DCO graceful degradation hierarchy can be given hardware-level safety guarantees through the Reflex layer.

The DCM also connects to the Mii Logical Architecture through the OCA, as described in OCA v1.0 Appendix B. The three-tier structure of the DCM — local tripartite cognition, inter-vessel belief coupling, and fleet-wide meta-cognitive authority — mirrors the three levels of the Mii hierarchy: the single-processor Mii core, the inter-chiplet adjunction interface, and the meta-cognitive coupling chiplet. Instantiating the DCM on a fleet of MiiPU-equipped vessels would therefore represent the first physical realisation of a Distributed Cognitive Orchestration system built on Mii silicon, a long-term research objective of this programme.

